            "rationale": "Bounded machine E1/G1 source-role union accepted by genuine independently first-sealed A2/B2 whole original source/case review. Operative current1c/fd/a44 retain proton transfer, water-ion predominance and selected-ion detection; retained chloride/water cases plus three new complete Br/carbonate/ammonium DE/EN synthetic witnesses cover the named six-ion intentions only. A: The whole original contextual Nachweisreaktionen row has concrete qualitative-ion intentions on45. Current selected a44 hosts retained chloride plus three new bounded Br/carbonate/ammonium cases, while current selected1c/fd and the two unchanged calibrated proton-reaction cases retain both water-ion intentions. All three union goals are actual current targets in all four BB/BE GK/LK scopes. The source union need not route through old invisible d2/413, does not add9dee applicability, does not infer original salt pairing, and does not promote written models to actual experiment completion. B: Whole a44 DE/EN includes experimental selected-ion detection, salt and salt-mixture qualitative composition, acidic/basic solutions and everyday-label checks. The retained complete chloride cases cover controlled pure salt and mixture/label/acid-base limitations; the three new complete cases add the specifically missing Br/CO3/NH4 intentions without promising universal ion identification or quantities. Together they support the intended selected-ion components. They do not newly certify the entire goal, actual practical execution or all source duties. Original Q3 source/stage/course and binding practical intent remain unchanged. Not whole a44 P approval, performed experiment, whole Q3 source completion, B477 compound closure, whole481 closure or human approval. Seals: curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-08/chemie-b014-b477-four-ion-intentions-targeted-independent-a-20261008-v4/four-ion-three-whole-cases-two-source-unions.independent-a.first-verdict.freeze.json; curricu