                "fullOperatorReasoningVerbatim": {
                  "atLeastOneDrugGroup": "The materials consistently use the salicylate group, ASA with salicylic-acid reference, rather than unrelated isolated medicine facts. One exemplary group satisfies the minimum without claiming all drug classes.",
                  "researchAndDevelopment": "A controlled supplied cell-free comparison supports only a bounded next development decision; the second case poses a stability/process development question and requires causal controls after contradictory scale findings.",
                  "laboratoryAndLargeScaleManufacture": "The reaction/work-up distinction, supplied ASA formation, scale-dependent heat-removal ratio, normalized formulation/hydrolysis outcomes and uncertainty/quality checks explicitly connect the small and plant stages.",
                  "marketing": "Finite accepted supply, demand, contribution versus profit, nonrepresentative survey, evidence limits and bounded internal product statements are connected to chemical findings.",
                  "connectedCoverage": "Whole-chain account and changed-finding feedback are required in both nonisomorphic cases. Coverage does not depend on a broad pharmacy parent, dosage-form fragments or presumed practical observations."
                },
